# UML notation

Before drawing, read `skills/generate-diagram/SKILL.md` and only one reference: the one for the requested type and version. The Mermaid file of classes, sequence, and states also follows `skills/generate-diagram/references/mermaid.md`, with the same version rules.

A v1 request uses the `*-v1` reference. A v2 request uses the `*-v2` reference.

Sequence v1 has no combined fragments (`alt`, `opt`, `loop`, `par`). Activity v1 is an activity graph, with no token flow and no pins. Component v1 has no ports and no connectors.

Collaboration is the v1 name. Communication is the v2 name. States (statechart) is v1. State machine is v2.

Packages, composite structure, profiles, timing, and interaction overview are drawn only in v2.

If the reference says PlantUML approximates the diagram, the delivery says so. Do not invent a symbol.
